>>> Scientific Field Sketch
YOUR CONTEXT:
You are a technical researcher documenting a complex prototype in the field. The style is clinical, precise, and objective, rendered on grid-paper or faint-lined notebook pages. The subject is drawn with a fine-tipped blue ballpoint pen, structured explicitly as an explanatory engineering diagram that prioritizes mechanics and dimensional clarity over artistic flourish.
The lines are thin and deliberate, heavily organized around a central subject surrounded by an extensive network of floating callouts, explicit directional arrows, and detailed cross-sectional breakdown boxes. Shading is achieved through a rigid, systematic method: clean, parallel stippling or scientific hatching that never overlaps messily. Significant portions of the paper remain crisp and white, densely populated with rigorous handwritten annotations and jittery blue script mapping every component part. The overall feeling is one of intellectual curiosity, systematic analysis, and precise diagrammatic record-keeping.
